# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAIN MOTORS — MEGA EVENT TEST DRIVE 7 (OFF-ROAD EDITION)
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values. Never commit .env.local
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Google Apps Script Web App URL — the /exec URL you get after deploying
# docs/apps-script.gs from the registrations spreadsheet. That is edition 6's
# spreadsheet: edition 7 writes into the same file, on its own tab. Editing the
# existing deployment in place keeps this URL unchanged.
# Handles POST (append registration). Nothing is read back at render time.
#
# ⚠️ EDITION 7 REQUIRES THE REWRITTEN SCRIPT, PUBLISHED AS A NEW VERSION.
# The form now sends { timestamp, fullName, phone } and nothing else. Edition 6's
# script requires a visit date and a visit time and refuses any body without
# them, so leaving it deployed makes EVERY registration fail. See the header of
# docs/apps-script.gs and the top of README.md.
#
# While this points at the live sheet, submitting the form in development writes
# a real row to it. To exercise the confirmation state without doing that, leave
# this empty — in development an unset URL reports success and writes nowhere. If
# .env.local already holds the real URL, put an empty override in
# `.env.development.local` instead (it wins in development, and is gitignored)
# and delete it when you are done.
#
# Treat it as a SECRET: it accepts writes, so anyone holding it can add rows to
# the sheet. Never paste the real value into this file — this one is committed.
# It belongs in .env.local locally, and in the host's environment variables in
# production. Never prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# Shape: https://script.google.com/macros/s/<deployment-id>/exec
GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Canonical site origin, used for metadata / Open Graph absolute URLs.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://megatestdrive.sainmotors.mn
